  "rules": [
    "Correct for severe downward bias: The model consistently overestimates prices by 5-10 EUR after the mid-August peak (73 EUR), failing to anticipate the structural drop to the low 60s.",
    "Adjust for momentum lag: The model exhibits a slow mean-reversion response, predicting a flat or slightly rising trajectory while the true market trend is a sharp, sustained decline.",
    "Incorporate sentiment sensitivity: When sentiment history shows negative values (e.g., -0.25), the model fails to reduce forecasts sufficiently; apply a steeper downward adjustment to the baseline forecast.",
    "Reduce overshoot on recovery attempts: The model predicts a gradual recovery in late September (rising to 68+), whereas the true outcome shows a volatile, lower-range consolidation (60-65); flatten the forecast tail.",
    "Apply volatility dampening: The model assumes a smooth path; real outcomes show high volatility with sharp intrahorizon drops (e.g., 70 to 66) that the model misses entirely."
  ]
}
